window.IELTS_BANK.speaking = [{"id":"new-0","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Do you have a bike now?","answer":"Yes, I do have a bike now. I use it mainly for short trips around my neighborhood, like going to the supermarket or visiting friends. It's a great way to stay active and avoid traffic."},{"id":"new-1","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Did you have a bike when you were young?","answer":"Yes, I had a bike when I was young. I used to ride it around the park with my friends, and it was one of my favorite activities. It gave me a sense of freedom and adventure."},{"id":"new-2","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Do you think riding bikes is popular in your country?","answer":"Yes, riding bikes is quite popular in China, especially in big cities. Many people use shared bikes for short trips because it's convenient and environmentally friendly. Plus, it's a great way to avoid traffic and get some exercise."},{"id":"new-3","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Do you often take coins with you?","answer":"Not really, I don't often carry coins with me. I usually prefer to use my debit card or mobile payments for convenience. Coins can be a bit heavy and cumbersome to carry around."},{"id":"new-4","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Have you collected coins?","answer":"Yes, I used to collect coins when I was a child. I was fascinated by different designs and shapes, especially foreign coins. It was a fun hobby that helped me learn about different cultures."},{"id":"new-5","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Is it convenient to use coins?","answer":"Not really, using coins isn't that convenient nowadays. Many places prefer digital payments, and coins can be a hassle to manage. They tend to pile up and make your wallet heavy."},{"id":"new-6","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Do you use coins in your daily life?","answer":"Not much, actually. Nowadays, I mostly use digital payments or credit cards for daily transactions. Coins have become less common for me, but I still keep some around just in case I need them for small purchases or parking meters."},{"id":"new-7","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Did you use coins as a child?","answer":"Yes, I used coins a lot when I was a child. They were handy for buying snacks from the local shop or for taking the bus. I remember saving up coins in a piggy bank, which was a fun way to learn about saving money."},{"id":"new-8","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Are the roads in the area where you live busy?","answer":"Yes, the roads in my area are quite busy, especially during rush hours. There’s a lot of traffic because it's a popular neighborhood with many shops and businesses. You often hear honking and see people rushing around."},{"id":"new-9","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"How do people cross the road in the city where you live?","answer":"In my city, people usually cross the road at designated crosswalks or traffic lights. However, some people also jaywalk when they're in a hurry, which can be dangerous. Most of the time, drivers are quite cautious and slow down for pedestrians."},{"id":"new-10","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"How is the condition of the roads in your city?","answer":"The condition of the roads in my city is generally good, but there are some areas with potholes and uneven surfaces. The city government repairs them regularly, but it can take some time. Overall, they're manageable for daily commutes."},{"id":"new-11","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Do you think the roads in your city need improvement?","answer":"Yes, I think the roads in my city could use some improvement, especially in the older parts of town. Better maintenance and more bike lanes would help a lot. Also, improving the drainage system would prevent flooding during heavy rains."},{"id":"new-12","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"How many roads are there in your neighborhood?","answer":"There aren’t too many roads in my neighborhood, just a few quiet streets. Most of them are lined with trees, and they’re usually not too busy. It’s a pretty peaceful area, so you don’t hear much traffic noise. I really like the calm vibe around here."},{"id":"new-13","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Do you like perfume? Why?","answer":"Yes, I do like perfume. It adds a nice touch to my daily routine and makes me feel more confident. Plus, a good scent can leave a lasting impression on others."},{"id":"new-14","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Do you have many bottles of perfume? Why?","answer":"I have a few bottles of perfume, but not too many. I like to have different scents for different occasions. It’s nice to switch things up depending on my mood or the event."},{"id":"new-15","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Would you ever give perfume as a gift?","answer":"Yes, I would definitely consider giving perfume as a gift. It’s a classic choice and can be very meaningful if you pick the right scent. It’s something that people can use and appreciate."},{"id":"new-16","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Which means of transport is convenient?","answer":"In big cities, the subway is probably the most convenient. It’s fast, avoids traffic, and has stations all over the city. You can get to almost anywhere without much hassle."},{"id":"new-17","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Which means of transport is expensive?","answer":"Taxis and ride-sharing services tend to be the most expensive, especially for long distances. Air travel can also be pricey, particularly if you’re booking last minute."},{"id":"new-18","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"What are the advantages of using public transport?","answer":"Public transport is cost-effective and eco-friendly. It reduces the number of cars on the road, helping to decrease traffic congestion. Plus, it’s a great way to reduce your carbon footprint."},{"id":"new-19","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Do you enjoy watching funny movies?","answer":"Yes, I really enjoy watching funny movies. They always lighten my mood and help me relax after a long day. I think it's great to have a good laugh and forget about stress for a while."},{"id":"new-20","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Do you think you are a funny person?","answer":"I like to think I have a good sense of humor and can make people laugh sometimes. I enjoy joking around with my friends and making them smile. I wouldn't say I'm the funniest person, but I do try to keep things light-hearted."},{"id":"new-21","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Do you always laugh at funny things?","answer":"Most of the time, I do laugh at funny things. I love a good joke or a funny story. Sometimes, even little things can make me chuckle, like a funny meme or a silly situation."},{"id":"new-22","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"What is the view like around the place where you live?","answer":"The view around where I live is quite nice. There are a few parks nearby, and I can see some greenery and trees from my window. It's a calm and peaceful neighborhood, which makes it a pleasant place to relax."},{"id":"new-23","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Have you seen an unforgettable view?","answer":"Yes, I once saw an unforgettable view when I visited a mountain range at sunrise. The sky was painted in shades of pink and orange, and the mist over the mountains made it look like a scene from a painting. It was truly breathtaking."},{"id":"new-24","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Will you take photos if you see a good view?","answer":"Definitely! If I see a good view, I love to capture it with my camera. Taking photos is a great way to remember beautiful moments and share them with friends and family."},{"id":"new-25","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Did you do a lot of teamwork when you were a child?","answer":"Yes, I did quite a bit of teamwork as a child, especially in school. We had group projects and sports activities that required us to collaborate and communicate with each other. It was a great way to learn about working with others and building friendships."},{"id":"new-26","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Do you like teamwork?","answer":"Yes, I generally like teamwork because it allows people to combine their strengths and come up with better ideas. It’s also a great way to learn from others and improve my own skills. However, it can sometimes be challenging if people don’t work well together."},{"id":"new-27","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Have you teamed up with someone else before?","answer":"Yes, I have teamed up with others many times, both in school and at work. I’ve worked on group projects, participated in team sports, and collaborated on various tasks. These experiences have helped me understand the importance of cooperation and communication."},{"id":"new-28","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"What do you learn from working in a team?","answer":"Working in a team teaches me how to communicate effectively, listen to different opinions, and respect others' ideas. It also helps me develop problem-solving skills and learn how to work towards a common goal. Overall, teamwork is a great way to grow both personally and professionally."},{"id":"new-29","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"What do you dislike about teamwork?","answer":"One thing I dislike about teamwork is when not everyone puts in the same amount of effort. It can be frustrating when some team members don’t pull their weight or when there are disagreements that slow down progress. But I try to stay positive and focus on finding solutions."},{"id":"new-30","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"What films do you like?","answer":"I enjoy a wide range of films, but I’m particularly fond of action and adventure movies. They’re exciting and keep me on the edge of my seat. I also like movies with a good storyline and strong characters."},{"id":"new-31","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Did you often watch films when you were a child?","answer":"Yes, I watched a lot of films when I was a child. My family used to have movie nights every weekend. It was a great way to spend time together, and I always looked forward to it."},{"id":"new-32","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Do you think going to the cinema is a good way to spend time with friends?","answer":"Definitely! Going to the cinema is a fun way to hang out with friends. You can enjoy a movie together and then chat about it afterward, which makes for a great shared experience."},{"id":"new-33","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Do you like to talk with others?","answer":"Yes, I do enjoy talking with others. I find it interesting to learn about different perspectives and share experiences. It’s a great way to build connections and make new friends."},{"id":"new-34","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Do you like to talk a lot with others?","answer":"It depends on the situation. I like to talk a lot when I’m with close friends or family, but in larger groups, I tend to listen more. I think a good balance between talking and listening is important."},{"id":"new-35","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Did you like to talk with others when you were a child?","answer":"Yes, I loved talking with others when I was a child. I was very curious and always asked a lot of questions. I enjoyed learning new things and making friends through conversations."},{"id":"new-36","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Do you like eating fish?","answer":"Yes, I really enjoy eating fish. It’s healthy and there are various ways to cook it. My favourite is grilled fish with some herbs and lemon."},{"id":"new-37","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Have you ever been fishing?","answer":"Yes, I’ve been fishing a few times. It’s a relaxing activity, especially when you’re out on a boat. I don’t always catch something, but it’s fun just to be out in nature."},{"id":"new-38","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Is fishing a very popular activity in your country?","answer":"Fishing is quite popular in my country, especially in coastal and rural areas. Many people enjoy it as a weekend hobby, and it’s also a big part of the local culture in some regions."},{"id":"new-39","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"What free time activities are popular with people in your country?","answer":"In my country, a lot of people enjoy going to cafes with friends, watching movies, or spending time outdoors in parks. Many also like to exercise, whether that’s jogging or going to the gym. On weekends, some prefer to visit malls for shopping or just to relax."},{"id":"new-40","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"What do you do when you have free time?","answer":"When I have some free time, I usually read books or catch up on my favorite TV series. I also like to go for a walk to clear my head. If I have more time, I might meet up with friends for a meal."},{"id":"new-41","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"What is the difference between the way people spend their free time now and in the past?","answer":"In the past, people spent more time doing outdoor activities or simple hobbies like reading and knitting. Nowadays, many people spend their free time on their phones or watching shows online. Technology has definitely changed how we relax and entertain ourselves."},{"id":"new-42","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Do you like making friends?","answer":"Yeah, I do enjoy making new friends. It’s always interesting to meet people with different backgrounds and perspectives. Plus, it’s nice to have more people to share experiences with. I find that it helps me grow as a person."},{"id":"new-43","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Did you make a lot of friends when you were a child?","answer":"Not really, I was actually a bit shy when I was a kid. I had a small group of close friends, and we used to play together all the time. It wasn’t until later that I became more outgoing and started making more friends."},{"id":"new-44","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Have you ever made any new friends recently?","answer":"Yeah, I’ve made a few new friends recently. I joined a local club, and it’s been a great way to meet new people. We usually hang out on weekends and have fun together."},{"id":"new-45","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"What do you often talk about with your new friends?","answer":"We talk about all sorts of things, from work and hobbies to travel and future plans. Sometimes, we just share funny stories or talk about things happening in the news. It’s nice to have different conversations depending on the mood."},{"id":"new-46","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Should you share your secrets with your friends?","answer":"I think it depends on how much you trust the person. If you’re really close and feel comfortable, it’s okay to share some personal things. But I wouldn’t share every secret with every friend – some things are better kept private."},{"id":"new-47","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Do you have a favourite teacher?","answer":"Yes, I have a favorite teacher from high school. She taught English and always made the class interesting and engaging. She had a way of explaining things that really helped me understand and enjoy the subject more."},{"id":"new-48","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Would you like to work as a teacher?","answer":"I think working as a teacher would be rewarding because you get to help students learn and grow. It seems like a meaningful job where you can make a real difference in people's lives. Plus, it's a great way to share your knowledge and passion with others."},{"id":"new-49","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Are you still in touch with your primary school teachers?","answer":"Not really, I lost touch with most of my primary school teachers over the years. I sometimes wonder how they are doing, but I haven't had the chance to reconnect. It would be nice to catch up with them someday."},{"id":"new-50","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"What is your favorite place to study?","answer":"I like studying at a quiet café near my house. It has a cozy atmosphere, and I can focus well there. Plus, the coffee keeps me energized when I need it."},{"id":"new-51","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Do you prefer to study at home or in a library?","answer":"I usually prefer studying at home because it’s more comfortable. I can take breaks whenever I want, and all my study materials are within reach. But sometimes, the library helps me stay more disciplined."},{"id":"new-52","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Do you prefer to work at home or in the workplace?","answer":"I prefer working in the office because it’s easier to collaborate with colleagues. However, working from home has its perks, like avoiding the commute. It really depends on what tasks I need to focus on."},{"id":"new-53","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe an old friend you didn't contact for a long time and got in contact with again.","answer":"I recently reconnected with an old friend named Lisa, who I hadn’t spoken to in years. We met in high school and quickly became close friends, bonding over our love for books and movies. However, after graduating, we lost touch because we went to different universities in different cities. Life got busy, and we just drifted apart. A few months ago, I stumbled upon her profile on social media and decided to send her a message. To my surprise, she replied right away, and we picked up right where we left off. It felt so good to talk to her again and catch up on each other’s lives. I realized how much I had missed our conversations and her sense of humor. Reconnecting with her reminded me of the importance of keeping in touch with old friends."},{"id":"new-54","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe a person who always has strong opinions.","answer":"One person I know who always has strong opinions is my colleague, Mark. I met him at my current job a few years ago, and we’ve worked on several projects together. Mark is someone who never hesitates to express his thoughts, no matter how controversial they might be. He’s very passionate about his beliefs and isn’t afraid to challenge others if he disagrees with them. I think he’s opinionated because he reads a lot and stays well-informed about current events, which makes him confident in his views. Sometimes, his strong opinions can be a bit overwhelming, especially during meetings, but I also appreciate that he’s honest and straightforward. He adds a lot of energy to discussions and often brings up points that others might not consider."},{"id":"new-55","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe a person who has chosen a career in the medical field.","answer":"A person I know who has chosen a career in the medical field is my cousin, Lisa. Lisa and I grew up together, and I've always admired her dedication and passion for helping others. She decided to become a doctor after volunteering at a local hospital during her high school years. She saw firsthand the impact that good medical care can have on people’s lives, and this inspired her to pursue a career in medicine. She wanted to make a difference and help those in need. I feel incredibly proud of her because becoming a doctor requires a lot of hard work, commitment, and sacrifice. She has faced many challenges, but her determination and genuine desire to help others keep her going. I think she’s a true role model for anyone considering a career in healthcare."},{"id":"new-56","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe a person who likes to make things by hand (e.g. toys, furniture).","answer":"I’d like to talk about my friend Emily. She loves to make things by hand, especially toys and small pieces of furniture. Emily is incredibly creative and enjoys using her hands to craft unique items. She likes to make things by hand because she finds it therapeutic and satisfying to see a project come to life from start to finish. She also appreciates the personal touch that handmade items have, which makes them more special than something bought from a store. I really admire Emily for her dedication and passion for her craft. It’s inspiring to see someone put so much love and effort into what they do, and her creations always have a warmth and charm that you can’t find in mass-produced products."},{"id":"new-57","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe a person who likes to read a lot.","answer":"My friend Sarah is someone who loves to read a lot. She always has a book with her, no matter where she goes. Sarah enjoys reading a wide range of genres, but her favorites are mystery novels and historical fiction. I know she likes to read because she often talks about the latest book she’s reading and shares interesting facts or stories she’s learned. She even has a big bookshelf at home filled with all the books she has read over the years. I think Sarah likes to read because it allows her to escape into different worlds and learn about new things. She says it helps her relax and unwind after a long day, and I can see how happy it makes her."},{"id":"new-58","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe a place in your city where you have seen wild animals.","answer":"There’s a place in my city called Green Park where I’ve seen wild animals. It's located on the outskirts of town, away from the busy city center. The park has a large natural reserve area where various animals like squirrels, rabbits, and even some deer roam freely. I’ve also spotted different species of birds and the occasional fox. Green Park is quite popular among nature lovers and photographers, so it can get a bit crowded on weekends. However, because the park is so large, you can still find quiet spots to observe the wildlife. I always feel a sense of peace and connection with nature when I visit. It’s a great escape from the hustle and bustle of city life, and I love watching the animals in their natural habitat."},{"id":"new-59","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe an ideal and perfect place where you would like to stay, e.g. a house or an apartment.","answer":"My ideal place to stay would be a cozy house by the beach, somewhere along the coast in southern Spain. The house would have a simple, elegant design with large windows that let in plenty of natural light and offer a stunning view of the ocean. It would be surrounded by a small garden filled with colorful flowers and a few fruit trees. Inside, there would be an open living space with a modern kitchen, a comfortable reading nook, and a spacious balcony where I could relax and enjoy the sea breeze. One special feature would be a private path leading directly to the beach, perfect for early morning walks. This place would be ideal for me because I love being close to nature, especially the ocean. It would provide a peaceful and inspiring environment where I could unwind and feel truly at home."},{"id":"new-60","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe a crowded place you've been to.","answer":"A crowded place I’ve been to is the Great Wall of China during the Golden Week holiday. I visited it last October with a group of friends. We chose to go during this time because we thought the autumn scenery would be beautiful, but we didn’t anticipate how packed it would be. When we arrived, the place was filled with tourists from all over the country and the world. We spent most of the day slowly making our way along the wall, taking pictures, and enjoying the incredible views despite the crowds. Although it was overwhelming at times with so many people around, I still felt a sense of awe and wonder. Being at such a historical and iconic site, even amidst the chaos, was a memorable experience. It made me appreciate the rich history and cultural significance of the Great Wall."},{"id":"new-61","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe a cultural place that you would like to learn the culture there.","answer":"A cultural place I would love to explore is the Louvre Museum in Paris, France. I’ve known about this iconic museum since I was a child, through books, documentaries, and stories from friends who have visited. The Louvre is home to an incredible collection of art and artifacts from different cultures and historical periods, such as the Mona Lisa and the Venus de Milo. You can learn so much there about European art history, the evolution of different artistic movements, and the cultural influences that shaped them. I am particularly interested in understanding the French Renaissance period and how art reflects the social and political contexts of its time. I would like to learn the culture there because it offers a deep dive into the rich heritage of Europe, and visiting such a world-renowned museum would be both inspiring and educational."},{"id":"new-62","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe someone's room where you enjoy spending time.","answer":"I love spending time in my friend Anna’s room. It’s cozy and beautifully decorated with lots of warm colors and soft lighting. Her room has a comfy sofa piled with cushions, a huge bookshelf filled with interesting novels, and a small desk where she works on her art projects. There’s also a large window with a great view of the garden, which lets in plenty of natural light. When I’m there, I enjoy reading one of her books, chatting with her, or just relaxing and looking out at the garden. The atmosphere is always calm and inviting, and her taste in decor makes it feel like a little retreat from the world. That’s why I always look forward to hanging out there."},{"id":"new-63","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe a public garden or park.","answer":"There’s a park near my house called East Coast Park. It’s right by the sea, so there’s always a nice breeze, and you can hear the sound of the waves. The park is huge, with plenty of spots to relax, have a picnic, or ride bikes. I usually go there once or twice a month, especially on weekends. Every time I visit, I feel calm and refreshed because it's a great escape from the busy city life."},{"id":"new-64","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe a small shop or store you often go to.","answer":"There’s a small bakery I visit quite often near my apartment. It’s just a five-minute walk from my place, which makes it really convenient. The last time I went there was actually last weekend. I usually stop by once or twice a week to grab a coffee and some fresh pastries. The bakery has this really warm and cozy atmosphere, and the staff are always friendly, which makes me feel welcome. I keep going back because their bread and pastries are always fresh, and I love supporting local businesses. Plus, it’s a nice break from the bigger, more crowded stores in the area."},{"id":"new-65","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe the most expensive item you have ever bought.","answer":"The most expensive item I have ever bought is a high-end laptop. I purchased it about a year ago from an electronics store in Beijing. I needed a reliable device for my work as an IELTS teacher and for personal projects like writing and video editing. I use it every day for lesson planning, conducting online classes, and creating educational content. I decided to buy this laptop because my previous one was slow and frequently crashed, which was frustrating and unproductive. I chose a model with a powerful processor, a high-resolution screen, and plenty of storage to ensure it could handle all my tasks smoothly. Although it was a significant investment, it has proven to be worth every penny because it has made my work more efficient and enjoyable."},{"id":"new-66","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe a traditional food at a traditional festival or a special event in your country.","answer":"One traditional food that I love is mooncakes, which are eaten during the Mid-Autumn Festival in China. Mooncakes are small, round pastries that have a thick filling, usually made of red bean paste, lotus seed paste, or salted egg yolks. They are often beautifully decorated with patterns on top and sometimes filled with nuts and seeds. Mooncakes are usually baked until golden brown and have a rich, sweet flavor. We eat them while celebrating the festival with family, enjoying the full moon, and appreciating the time spent together. I like mooncakes because they remind me of family gatherings and the joy of celebrating our culture. Plus, they’re delicious and come in so many varieties!"},{"id":"new-67","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe a picture or photo in your home that you like.","answer":"There’s a family photo hanging in my living room that I really love. It’s a picture of my parents, my siblings, and me during a holiday we took a few years ago. We’re all standing by the beach, smiling, with the sunset in the background. I placed it in the living room because it reminds me of a happy time we spent together. My dad actually took the photo, which makes it even more special. This picture is meaningful to me because it captures a rare moment when we were all relaxed and enjoying each other’s company."},{"id":"new-68","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe an online video where you learned something new.","answer":"I recently watched an online video on YouTube about basic cooking techniques. I watched it last month at home, during the weekend when I had some free time. The video was a tutorial by a professional chef who demonstrated how to chop vegetables correctly, cook perfect pasta, and make a simple sauce from scratch. I decided to watch it because I wanted to improve my cooking skills and start preparing healthier meals at home. From this video, I learned some useful knife skills, such as how to hold a knife properly and different cutting techniques. It also taught me the importance of timing and seasoning in cooking, which has made a big difference in the dishes I make now. Overall, it was an eye-opening experience, and it boosted my confidence in the kitchen."},{"id":"new-69","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe a challenge you faced that you thought was rather difficult.","answer":"One of the most challenging situations I faced was when I had to deliver a presentation in English at an international conference last year in Shanghai. Although I’ve been studying English for years, speaking in front of a large audience, especially one filled with native speakers, was incredibly daunting. I had prepared my speech thoroughly, but as the day approached, I began to doubt my language skills and my ability to engage the audience. It felt like an uphill battle because I was worried about making mistakes or not being understood. At the time, I was filled with anxiety and self-doubt. However, I knew this was a great opportunity for personal growth. Despite the fear, I pushed myself to go through with it, and afterward, I felt a great sense of accomplishment. It taught me the value of stepping out of my comfort zone and facing my fears head-on."},{"id":"new-70","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe a prize you have received.","answer":"A prize that stands out in my memory is a medal I received for completing a marathon a couple of years ago. I got it in the fall of 2021 when I participated in my first-ever marathon in Beijing. To earn this medal, I had to push myself both physically and mentally for months. I remember waking up early every morning to train, slowly increasing my distance each week, and building my stamina. Crossing the finish line was a moment of pure joy and relief, but also disbelief—I couldn’t believe I had actually done it! Receiving the medal was such a rewarding experience. It wasn’t just a piece of metal; it symbolized all the hard work, determination, and perseverance I had put into reaching my goal. It gave me a deep sense of pride and accomplishment."},{"id":"new-71","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe a film that you watched recently.","answer":"A few weeks ago, I watched a movie called Oppenheimer. It's a historical drama about the life of J. Robert Oppenheimer, the scientist behind the creation of the atomic bomb. I saw it at a cinema with a friend, and we both really enjoyed it. The film was intense and thought-provoking, especially how it showed the ethical dilemmas faced by scientists during that time. I wanted to discuss it because it wasn’t just entertaining, but it also made me think deeply about the impact of science on society. I’d definitely recommend it to anyone who enjoys history and complex characters."},{"id":"new-72","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe a time when you answered a phone call from someone you didn't know in a public place.","answer":"I remember a time when I answered a phone call from an unknown number while I was at a café. It happened last month when I was having coffee and reading a book. I picked up the call, and it turned out to be a woman who had dialed the wrong number. She asked if she was speaking to 'John,' but I told her she had the wrong person. She apologized and explained that she was trying to reach a friend about an urgent matter. I responded politely, letting her know it was no problem, and she quickly hung up. The whole experience was a bit awkward because I was in a quiet public place, and I felt like people around me might be listening. However, it also made me realize the importance of being patient and understanding when such situations occur."},{"id":"new-73","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe something that made you feel confident.","answer":"One thing that made me feel confident was giving a presentation at work last year. It happened during an important meeting with our team and some senior managers. I had spent a lot of time preparing and researching the topic, and I knew the content inside out. When it was my turn to present, I felt a bit nervous at first, but as I started speaking and saw the positive reactions from the audience, my confidence grew. Successfully delivering the presentation and answering all the questions made me realize that I could communicate my ideas clearly and effectively. This experience boosted my self-esteem and helped me feel more self-assured in professional settings. I felt proud of myself and motivated to take on more challenges."},{"id":"new-74","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe a time when you lost a valuable item.","answer":"I remember losing my wallet last winter while I was traveling in Guangzhou. The wallet wasn’t just valuable because of the cash inside; it also held my ID, bank cards, and a few sentimental items like a photo of my family. It was worth around 500 yuan, but its sentimental value was priceless. I think I lost it when I was rushing to catch a train. I had placed it in the outer pocket of my bag, and somehow, in the chaos of getting through security, it must have slipped out. When I realized it was gone, I felt a wave of panic and frustration. I retraced my steps and asked the station staff, but it was nowhere to be found. It was a stressful experience, but it also taught me to be more careful and aware of my belongings, especially when traveling."},{"id":"new-75","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe a time when you asked someone for advice.","answer":"A time when I asked someone for advice was when I was considering a career change a couple of years ago. I turned to my mentor, Mr. Chen, who has always been a great source of wisdom and guidance. I sought his advice because I was feeling uncertain and anxious about leaving my stable job for a new opportunity that seemed risky but exciting. I explained my situation to him, and he listened carefully before giving his advice. He suggested that I weigh the pros and cons of both options and think about what would make me happiest in the long run. He also reminded me that taking calculated risks can lead to personal growth. I felt his advice was thoughtful and practical, and it helped me feel more confident in making my decision. I ultimately decided to take the new job, and I’ve been happier ever since."},{"id":"new-76","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe a party that you enjoyed.","answer":"Last month, I attended a birthday party for my best friend at a cozy rooftop café in the city. The party was small, with just a few close friends and family members. It was a surprise party, so the excitement in the air was palpable. We had a lot of fun playing games, sharing stories, and enjoying the delicious food. What made this party special was the warm atmosphere and the fact that everyone was there to celebrate someone we all cared about. I left the party feeling happy and grateful for such a wonderful time with friends."},{"id":"new-77","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe a time when you helped your family member.","answer":"Last year, I helped my sister when she was preparing for her university entrance exams. It was a stressful time for her, and she needed support with some subjects, especially math. I would sit with her every evening, going through practice questions and explaining difficult concepts. I helped her because I knew how important these exams were, and I wanted her to feel confident. It was a rewarding experience for me because, in the end, she passed her exams with flying colors. I felt proud that I could be there for her and make a difference."},{"id":"new-78","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (new)","question":"Describe an occasion when you received good service from a company or shop.","answer":"A few months ago, I went to a small electronics store to buy a new laptop. The staff was incredibly helpful, especially one employee who really knew his stuff. He patiently explained the differences between various models and even recommended a more affordable option that suited my needs perfectly. The store was located near my workplace, so it was very convenient. What really impressed me was how honest and friendly the service was. They weren’t just trying to sell me the most expensive product—they genuinely wanted to help me find the right laptop. That’s why I felt it was excellent service."},{"id":"old-0","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you like art?","answer":"I find great joy in art as it allows for personal enrichment, offers diverse forms of visual expression, and fosters a deeper appreciation for different cultures."},{"id":"old-1","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"How often do you go to art galleries?","answer":"I don't go to art galleries very often, maybe once or twice a year. It's usually when there's a special exhibit or if I'm traveling to a new city. I do enjoy the experience, but it's not something I seek out regularly."},{"id":"old-2","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you like visiting art galleries in your free time?","answer":"Visiting art galleries is delightful because they provide immersive experiences, serve as a source of artistic inspiration, and allow for extensive visual exploration."},{"id":"old-3","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you like modern or traditional art?","answer":"My preference leans towards modern art due to its innovative techniques and the contemporary themes it often explores, though I also value the historical depth of traditional art."},{"id":"old-4","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Would you like to be an artist?","answer":"I admire artists for their creative expression, but I don't aspire to be a professional artist. Engaging in art as a personal hobby, however, is something I consider."},{"id":"old-5","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"How often do you wear jewellery?","answer":"I wear jewellery occasionally, mostly on special occasions. It's not a daily accessory for me, but I do enjoy wearing it when the event calls for it."},{"id":"old-6","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"What types of jewellery do you like to buy?","answer":"I prefer buying timeless pieces that are made from high-quality materials. I like jewellery that makes a statement but can still be worn for many years."},{"id":"old-7","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you usually buy jewellery?","answer":"I don’t buy jewellery very often; I only purchase it occasionally when I find something that truly appeals to me. I prefer to invest in quality rather than quantity."},{"id":"old-8","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Have you ever bought any jewellery?","answer":"Yes, I’ve bought jewelry a few times, mostly as gifts for family or friends. I’m not really into wearing it myself, but I do appreciate how a nice piece can make a special occasion even more memorable."},{"id":"old-9","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Why do you think some people wear a piece of jewellery for a long time?","answer":"Many people wear a piece of jewellery for a long time because it holds sentimental value or personal significance. It might represent an important event or a loved one, and often, it also complements their personal style consistently."},{"id":"old-10","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"What made you excited during childhood?","answer":"Currently, I find excitement in achieving personal goals, spending quality time with loved ones, and pursuing hobbies that I'm passionate about, like reading or hiking."},{"id":"old-11","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"What makes you excited now?","answer":"I’m really excited about an upcoming trip I’ve planned. It’s been a while since I’ve traveled, so I’m looking forward to exploring new places and trying new things. The anticipation is definitely keeping me energized these days."},{"id":"old-12","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you prefer an exciting or a relaxing activity?","answer":"I usually prefer a relaxing activity, like reading or taking a walk. Life can get pretty hectic, so I enjoy winding down whenever I can. That said, I do appreciate exciting activities every now and then to shake things up."},{"id":"old-13","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Have you experienced anything exciting recently?","answer":"Recently, I've had some exciting adventures, like exploring new hiking trails and meeting interesting people from different backgrounds, which has been quite exhilarating."},{"id":"old-14","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Would you like to try some activities like rock climbing?","answer":"I think I’d be open to trying something like rock climbing, but I’d have to build up the courage first! It looks fun and challenging, and I do enjoy pushing myself to try new things, even if it’s a bit outside my comfort zone."},{"id":"old-15","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you think activities like scuba diving are exciting?","answer":"Absolutely! Scuba diving seems incredibly exciting. The idea of exploring the underwater world and seeing marine life up close would be such a thrilling experience. It’s definitely on my list of things I’d love to try one day."},{"id":"old-16","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you prefer to use a pen or pencil?","answer":"I prefer using a pen for its smooth writing experience and the clean look it gives to written text, although pencils are great for situations where you might need to erase and correct your work."},{"id":"old-17","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"When do you usually use a pen or pencil?","answer":"I use a pen mostly for taking notes and writing in formal documents where permanence is important. A pencil is my go-to for sketching, drafting, or any task where I might need to make corrections."},{"id":"old-18","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Has your school ever taught you how to use pencils?","answer":"Yes, my school did teach us how to use pencils when we were very young. We learned how to hold them properly and how to write neatly. It was one of those basic skills that everyone had to master early on."},{"id":"old-19","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Has someone ever taught you how to use a pen/pencil?","answer":"Yes, my parents and teachers both taught me how to use a pen and pencil. They showed me how to hold them correctly and guided me through my early writing practice. It was something they emphasized to ensure I developed good handwriting habits."},{"id":"old-20","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"When was the last time you bought a pen/pencil?","answer":"The last time I bought a pen was a few months ago. I needed a new one for taking notes, and I found a nice gel pen that writes smoothly. It’s actually become one of my favorites to use."},{"id":"old-21","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you think a pen or a pencil is a good gift?","answer":"Yes, a pen or pencil can be a thoughtful gift, especially if it's high-quality or beautifully crafted. They are both practical and personal, suitable for people of all ages and professions."},{"id":"old-22","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you think pen or pencil will still be popular in the future?","answer":"Despite the advancements in digital technology, I believe pens and pencils will remain popular due to their simplicity, reliability, and the tactile experience they offer. They have a timeless appeal that keeps them relevant even in a digital age."},{"id":"old-23","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you like watching the stars?","answer":"Yes, I enjoy watching the stars because it's such a peaceful activity that highlights the celestial beauty of the night sky and always fills me with a sense of wonder."},{"id":"old-24","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Have you ever learnt about outer space?","answer":"I've learned about outer space through various educational experiences, from school courses to documentaries. Understanding astronomical concepts and phenomena is fascinating and an ongoing learning journey."},{"id":"old-25","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Would you like to go to outer space in the future?","answer":"The idea of going to outer space is thrilling, and thanks to technological advancements, it might even become possible in the future. It's certainly an exciting adventure that I dream of experiencing."},{"id":"old-26","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Have you ever watched any movies about outer space?","answer":"Yes, I've watched many movies about outer space. Films like 'Interstellar' and 'Gravity' offer incredible cinematic journeys and present inspiring stories set against the backdrop of the vast cosmos."},{"id":"old-27","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you like wearing a T-shirt?","answer":"Yes, I enjoy wearing T-shirts because they are comfortable, casual, and versatile. They are perfect for many occasions and easy to pair with different types of clothing."},{"id":"old-28","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"How often do you wear a T-shirt?","answer":"I wear T-shirts pretty often, especially on weekends or when I’m just hanging out at home. They’re comfortable and easy to throw on, so I’d say I wear one at least a few times a week."},{"id":"old-29","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"What kinds of T-shirts do you like to wear?","answer":"I like to wear plain, solid-colored T-shirts most of the time. They’re versatile and go well with almost anything. I also enjoy graphic tees with simple designs or logos, especially if they have a cool or meaningful message."},{"id":"old-30","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you like T-shirts with pictures/patterns?","answer":"I do like T-shirts with pictures or patterns as they add visual interest and allow me to express my personal style. They can also be great conversation starters."},{"id":"old-31","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you think older people who wear T-shirts are fashionable?","answer":"Absolutely, older people can look very fashionable in T-shirts. Fashion is about personal choice and comfort, and T-shirts can be both stylish and age-appropriate."},{"id":"old-32","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Have you ever bought T-shirts at souvenir shops?","answer":"Yes, buying T-shirts as souvenirs on vacation is a great idea. They serve as practical gifts and memorable mementos of the places visited, often featuring iconic symbols or slogans from the destination."},{"id":"old-33","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you often stay up late?","answer":"I don't regularly stay up late, but occasionally it happens, especially if there's something specific that requires extra time or if I'm particularly engrossed in a book or project."},{"id":"old-34","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Is it easy to wake up in the morning if you stay up late?","answer":"It's usually quite challenging to wake up in the morning after staying up late. Staying up disrupts the normal sleep routine, which can affect how refreshed I feel the next day."},{"id":"old-35","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Did you stay up late often when you were younger?","answer":"When I was younger, I did stay up late more frequently. The youthful energy and having fewer responsibilities made it easier to recover from late nights."},{"id":"old-36","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"What do you usually do when you stay up late?","answer":"When I stay up late, it's usually because I'm either caught up in reading a good book, watching movies, or sometimes working on personal projects that require extended hours."},{"id":"old-37","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"What languages do you speak?","answer":"My native language is English, and I'm fluent in Spanish. I also have basic proficiency in French, which allows me to manage simple conversations."},{"id":"old-38","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"What languages have you learned at school?","answer":"Through my school curriculum, I learned Spanish and French. These language classes were part of my formal education, providing a good foundation in grammar and vocabulary."},{"id":"old-39","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Have you ever learnt about a foreign language?","answer":"Yes, I’ve learned a bit of a few foreign languages. I studied French in school for a few years, and I’ve also picked up some basic Spanish on my own. Learning languages is fascinating because it opens up new ways to connect with people and cultures."},{"id":"old-40","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you think it’s challenging to learn a foreign language?","answer":"Yes, learning a foreign language can be quite challenging. It requires a lot of dedication, practice, and patience, especially to grasp the cultural nuances and achieve fluency."},{"id":"old-41","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you think it’s necessary for Chinese students nowadays to learn foreign languages?","answer":"Yes, I think it’s necessary for Chinese students to learn foreign languages nowadays. In our increasingly globalized world, knowing a foreign language can provide more opportunities, whether in education, career, or even travel."},{"id":"old-42","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Are there many small businesses in China?","answer":"Yes, there are quite a few small businesses in my area, such as family-run restaurants, grocery stores, and handicraft shops. These small businesses add unique flavors and vibrancy to the community."},{"id":"old-43","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you know any small businesses?","answer":"Yes, I know a few small businesses in my area. There’s a cozy café run by a local family that serves great coffee and homemade pastries. I also know a boutique that sells unique, handmade clothing and accessories."},{"id":"old-44","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you prefer buying things from big companies or small businesses?","answer":"I prefer buying from small businesses as they often provide more personal service and quality products. It's also a way to support local entrepreneurs and the community."},{"id":"old-45","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you prefer buying things in supermarkets or small shops?","answer":"For daily necessities, supermarkets are more convenient. But for specialty items or bargaining, I prefer small shops which offer unique products and a more personal shopping experience."},{"id":"old-46","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Have you ever worked in any small businesses?","answer":"Yes, I’ve worked in a small business before. During college, I had a part-time job at a local bookstore. It was a great experience because I got to interact closely with customers and learn about running a business on a smaller scale."},{"id":"old-47","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Would you like to set up a small business?","answer":"Running a small business could be rewarding as you get to be your own boss and have a flexible schedule. However, it also comes with many challenges that require hard work and perseverance."},{"id":"old-48","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you like science?","answer":"Yes, I really enjoy science as it allows us to better understand the workings of the world around us. Science gives us an endless sense of curiosity and desire to explore."},{"id":"old-49","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Did you like learning science when you were young?","answer":"As a student, I had a keen interest in science subjects. The lively and interesting explanations from teachers gave me an initial appreciation and love for science."},{"id":"old-50","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you use science in your daily life?","answer":"Science is everywhere - many of the devices and products we use in daily life are the fruits of scientific advancements. Therefore, we are constantly applying scientific knowledge."},{"id":"old-51","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Is there any science you want to learn in the future?","answer":"In the future, I hope to continue learning about cutting-edge scientific fields such as artificial intelligence and quantum computing, to explore new frontiers of science."},{"id":"old-52","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Is it necessary for people to learn science?","answer":"Yes, I believe it’s necessary for people to learn science. Science helps us understand the world around us, from how things work to why certain events happen."},{"id":"old-53","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"What do you usually do on weekends?","answer":"On weekends, I like to relax and do fun activities. I often go outdoors for hiking or cycling. I also enjoy reading books and watching movies."},{"id":"old-54","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"What did you do last weekend?","answer":"Last weekend, I went to a nearby town with friends. We visited some interesting small shops and tried local foods. It was an enjoyable day trip."},{"id":"old-55","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you often work or study at weekends?","answer":"No, I try not to work or study too much on weekends. I prefer to use that time to rest and have fun. But sometimes I need to handle urgent tasks."},{"id":"old-56","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"What’s your favourite part of the weekend?","answer":"My favorite part is being able to live at my own pace, without work or study obligations. I can freely do whatever activities I enjoy."},{"id":"old-57","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you think weekends are important to you?","answer":"Yes, weekends are definitely important to me. They give me a chance to relax and recharge after a busy week."},{"id":"old-58","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you make plans for a weekend?","answer":"Yes, I usually make plans for the weekend, even if they’re just simple ones. I might schedule time to meet friends, run errands, or just plan to relax at home."},{"id":"old-59","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you like eating chocolate?","answer":"Yes, I really like eating chocolate. I especially enjoy rich, smooth dark chocolate. Chocolate is a delicious treat for me."},{"id":"old-60","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"How often do you eat chocolate?","answer":"I eat chocolate a couple of times a week, usually as a small treat after a meal or with a cup of coffee. I try not to overdo it, but it’s hard to resist when I’m craving something sweet."},{"id":"old-61","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Did you eat chocolate when you were a kid?","answer":"When I was a child, I often ate chocolate candies. Chocolate was one of my favorite snacks and brought me lots of joy."},{"id":"old-62","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"What’s your favourite flavour?","answer":"My favorite flavor is definitely dark chocolate. I love its rich, slightly bitter taste, and it feels a bit more sophisticated than sweeter options."},{"id":"old-63","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Have you ever given chocolate as a gift to others?","answer":"Yes, I’ve given chocolate as a gift many times. It’s a classic choice, especially for holidays or special occasions."},{"id":"old-64","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you think it’s good to give chocolate as a gift to others?","answer":"Chocolate makes a great gift for others, whether for holidays or ordinary days. Giving chocolate can bring happiness and surprise."},{"id":"old-65","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Why do you think chocolate is popular around the world?","answer":"I think chocolate is popular globally because of its unique flavor and texture that provides a pleasant experience. It also has some cultural roots."},{"id":"old-66","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you always bring a lot of keys with you?","answer":"Yes, I usually carry several keys with me, like house keys, car keys and office keys. I keep them all on a key ring."},{"id":"old-67","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Have you ever lost your keys?","answer":"I have lost my keys before. That experience taught me to be more careful about keeping track of my keys."},{"id":"old-68","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"How often do you go to a library?","answer":"I go to the library quite often, maybe every two or three weeks. The quiet environment is great for reading and studying."},{"id":"old-69","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Did you often go to a library when you were a child?","answer":"Yes, I went to libraries frequently as a child. It was an important way for me to access knowledge and information."},{"id":"old-70","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do Chinese children often go to libraries?","answer":"Nowadays, Chinese children do visit libraries often, though more for studying purposes rather than leisure reading."},{"id":"old-71","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Did Chinese people often go to libraries when they were young?","answer":"In the past, not as many Chinese people went to libraries when they were young compared to today. Libraries weren’t as widespread or accessible, especially in smaller towns."},{"id":"old-72","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you think it’s necessary to have libraries in university?","answer":"Yes, I think it’s absolutely necessary to have libraries in universities. They provide essential resources for students, like academic books, research materials, and a quiet place to study."},{"id":"old-73","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Would you like to work in a library?","answer":"Working in a library could be very meaningful, helping others gain knowledge and spread culture. If I had the opportunity, I would enjoy that job."},{"id":"old-74","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"When did you start using the internet?","answer":"I started using the internet in the late 1990s when dial-up connections were still common. The internet speeds were very slow back then."},{"id":"old-75","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"How often do you use the internet?","answer":"Nowadays, I use the internet every day for work, study, entertainment and social purposes. The internet has become part of our daily lives."},{"id":"old-76","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you think people always use mobile phones?","answer":"Yes, I think people use mobile phones almost constantly these days. Whether it’s for staying connected, browsing social media, or just passing the time, our phones have become an integral part of daily life."},{"id":"old-77","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you think you spend too much time on the internet/your phone?","answer":"Yes, I sometimes feel like I spend too much time on my phone, especially on social media and mindless scrolling. It can be easy to lose track of time, and I’m trying to be more mindful about setting limits and taking breaks to do other things."},{"id":"old-78","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"What are the differences between reading things on the phone and paper?","answer":"Reading on a phone is convenient because you can access a wide range of content instantly, and it’s easy to carry around. However, reading on paper feels more immersive, and it’s less straining on the eyes."},{"id":"old-79","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"How does the Internet influence people?","answer":"The internet has transformed how people access information and resources. It also facilitates communication and connections between people globally."},{"id":"old-80","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"On what occasions are you not allowed to use a mobile phone?","answer":"Using mobile phones is usually not permitted during events like exams, meetings or classes. This is to avoid distractions and prevent information leaks that could compromise the integrity of these occasions."},{"id":"old-81","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"How would you feel if there was no internet?","answer":"If there was no internet, I’d probably feel a bit lost at first because so much of my daily life relies on it—communication, work, entertainment, and even getting information."},{"id":"old-82","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you usually use numbers?","answer":"Yes, I use numbers in my daily life for tasks like shopping, budgeting, and scheduling."},{"id":"old-83","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Are you good at remembering phone numbers?","answer":"Yes, I use numbers in my daily life for tasks like shopping, budgeting, and scheduling. However, I don't use them extensively beyond basic calculations."},{"id":"old-84","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Are you good at maths?","answer":"I would say I'm decent at math. While it's not my strongest subject, I can manage basic calculations and understand fundamental concepts."},{"id":"old-85","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"What’s your favourite number?","answer":"My favorite number is 7. It's a lucky number in many cultures, and I've always associated it with positivity and good fortune."},{"id":"old-86","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Would you use numbers in your job (in the future)?","answer":"Yes, I’d likely use numbers in my job in the future. Whether it’s tracking progress, analyzing data, or managing finances, numbers play a crucial role in making informed decisions."},{"id":"old-87","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Is breakfast important for you?","answer":"Yes, breakfast is important to me. It helps me start the day with energy and focus. If I skip it, I usually feel sluggish and less productive throughout the morning."},{"id":"old-88","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"What’s your daily morning routine?","answer":"My daily morning routine usually involves waking up, having breakfast, and then getting ready for the day. I also like to take a few minutes to check my emails or review my schedule before heading out."},{"id":"old-89","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Is your morning routine the same as that when you were young?","answer":"No, my morning routine has changed a lot since I was young. Back then, I had more time to get ready, and I didn’t have as many responsibilities."},{"id":"old-90","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you want a different morning routine in the future?","answer":"Yes, I’d like to have a more relaxed morning routine in the future. I’d love to incorporate activities like morning exercise or meditation to start the day on a positive note."},{"id":"old-91","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Have you seen the news this morning?","answer":"No, I haven’t seen the news this morning yet. I usually catch up on the news later in the day when I have more time to sit down and read or watch it."},{"id":"old-92","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you often talk about the news with others?","answer":"Yes, I often talk about the news with others, especially with friends or colleagues. It’s a good way to stay informed and exchange different perspectives on current events."},{"id":"old-93","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Would you like to be a journalist in the future?","answer":"While I think being a journalist would be interesting, it’s not something I see myself doing in the future. I admire the work journalists do, but I prefer a career that allows me to teach and interact with people directly."},{"id":"old-94","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Which do you prefer, digital or paper books?","answer":"Personally, I prefer reading paper books. There's something about the tactile experience and the smell of the pages that enhances the reading experience for me."},{"id":"old-95","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"When do you usually read online?","answer":"I usually read online articles or e-books in my free time, particularly during breaks or before bedtime. I find it convenient to access a wide range of reading materials on platforms like Kindle, Wattpad, or various news websites."},{"id":"old-96","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"What are the benefits of reading e-books?","answer":"Reading e-books offers several benefits. First, they’re incredibly convenient; you can carry thousands of books on a single device, making it easy to read anywhere."},{"id":"old-97","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"What kinds of books do you like to read?","answer":"I enjoy reading a variety of books, but I’m particularly drawn to fiction, especially mysteries and thrillers. I also like reading non-fiction, such as biographies and self-improvement books."},{"id":"old-98","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Do you think people spend much time reading books?","answer":"I think it varies, but overall, many people today spend less time reading books compared to the past. With the rise of digital media, social media, and streaming services, people often turn to shorter, more immediate forms of entertainment."},{"id":"old-99","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"What do you often like to share with others?","answer":"I often like to share interesting articles, books, or music with others. If I come across something that I think a friend would enjoy or find useful, I love passing it along."},{"id":"old-100","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"What do you not share with others?","answer":"I tend not to share very personal details, like financial information or private thoughts, unless it’s with someone I trust deeply."},{"id":"old-101","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Did your family encourage/teach you to share something with others?","answer":"Yes, my parents taught me the importance of sharing when I was a child. They encouraged me to share toys, snacks, and experiences with others, emphasizing the value of generosity and cooperation in building relationships."},{"id":"old-102","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"What sports do/did you do at school?","answer":"When I was in school, I participated in several sports. I played basketball and enjoyed it because it was a great way to stay active and work as part of a team."},{"id":"old-103","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"What sports do you like?","answer":"I enjoy playing tennis. I find it challenging and rewarding, especially when I can play against a good opponent."},{"id":"old-104","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"What are the benefits of doing sports?","answer":"Doing sports offers many benefits. Physically, it helps improve fitness, build strength, and maintain a healthy weight. Mentally, sports can reduce stress, boost mood, and enhance concentration. Socially, participating in sports can help you make new friends, develop teamwork skills, and build confidence."},{"id":"old-105","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe a person who loves to buy something with low prices.","answer":"My aunt, Lisa, is a true bargain hunter. I've known her since I was a child, and she has always been the one to stretch her budget by finding the best deals. She mainly shops for clothes and kitchen gadgets, but she's always on the lookout for anything that promises value for money."},{"id":"old-106","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe a person you are happy to know.","answer":"The person I am truly happy to know is my colleague, Mr. Zhang. We met at the school where we both teach, and I've known him for about three years now. He has become both a mentor and a friend to me during this time."},{"id":"old-107","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe an actor/actress that you admire.","answer":"The actor I admire the most is Tom Hanks. I first came to know him through his role in the movie 'Forrest Gump,' which is one of my favorites. Since then, I've followed his career and watched many of his films, ranging from dramas to comedies."},{"id":"old-108","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe an interesting old person you’ve met.","answer":"I met Mr. Wang, a fascinating elderly man, at a community center two years ago. He was a retired teacher who had taught history for over 30 years. Our first conversation happened quite by accident during a local history exhibition at the center, where he was a volunteer guide."},{"id":"old-109","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe a person who thinks music is important.","answer":"The person I know who believes music is incredibly important and enjoys it immensely is my friend, Sarah. We met in college where we were both members of the music club, sharing our playlists and attending concerts together."},{"id":"old-110","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe someone (e.g. a famous person) who is a role model for young people.","answer":"The famous person who I believe could be a role model for young people is Malala Yousafzai. I first learned about her through her autobiography and numerous interviews she has given. Her advocacy for girls' education and her personal story have made headlines around the world."},{"id":"old-111","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe someone who gave you encouragement.","answer":"The person who encouraged me to achieve my goal is my mentor, Mr. Chen. He was my teacher during my university years and has continued to be a guiding figure in my professional life."},{"id":"old-112","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe a place (indoor or outdoors) that’s suitable for study.","answer":"My favorite place to study is the local library in my neighborhood. It’s a small, two-story building surrounded by a quiet garden, which helps create a peaceful environment ideal for studying."},{"id":"old-113","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe a city where you would like to stay for a short time.","answer":"The city where I want to stay for a short time is Kyoto, Japan. I plan to go there with my best friend, who shares my interest in Japanese culture and history."},{"id":"old-114","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe a city/town/village (not your hometown) you would like to live in.","answer":"I would recommend Vancouver, Canada, as a nice place to live. It's a coastal city that boasts a unique mix of urban development alongside natural landscapes."},{"id":"old-115","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe a place you’ve been to where things are expensive.","answer":"One place I've visited where things are notoriously expensive is the Ginza district in Tokyo, Japan. As I strolled through the immaculate streets lined with high-end shops and boutiques, I couldn't help but notice the extravagant window displays showcasing luxury goods from renowned brands."},{"id":"old-116","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe a place you visited where the air was not clean.","answer":"During a recent business trip to a major industrial city, I experienced firsthand the effects of poor air quality. As soon as I stepped off the plane, a thick haze enveloped the surroundings, obscuring the once-clear skyline."},{"id":"old-117","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe a tourist attraction that very few people visit but you think it is interesting.","answer":"Tucked away in a remote corner of our region lies a hidden gem, an off-the-beaten-path tourist attraction that few people venture to explore. This undiscovered treasure, nestled amidst rolling hills and winding roads, offers a unique and authentic experience for those willing to stray from the well-trodden tourist trails."},{"id":"old-118","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe an unusual meal that someone made for you.","answer":"One special meal that stands out in my memory was made by my grandmother. It was during the winter holidays when I was a child, and the entire family had gathered at her house. My grandmother is a wonderful cook, and she always takes pride in preparing delicious meals for her family."},{"id":"old-119","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe a piece of technology you own that is difficult to use.","answer":"In our rapidly evolving technological landscape, I recently acquired a cutting-edge gadget that promised to revolutionize my daily routine. However, despite its advanced features and sleek design, this particular piece of technology has proven to be a formidable challenge."},{"id":"old-120","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe something you own and want to replace now.","answer":"Among the various possessions that have accompanied me through life's journey, there is one particular item that holds a special place in my heart, yet has reached a point where it no longer serves its purpose effectively."},{"id":"old-121","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe an important plant in your country.","answer":"In my country, one important plant is the tea plant. Tea is cultivated extensively in regions with suitable climates, such as hillsides and mountainous areas. The tea plant typically has dark green leaves and produces small white flowers when in bloom."},{"id":"old-122","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe a new law that you would like to see/introduce in your country.","answer":"One new law that I would like to see in my country is mandatory recycling legislation. This law would require households and businesses to separate recyclable materials from their regular waste and provide recycling bins for collection."},{"id":"old-123","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe a sport you’ve watched/seen and you would like to try.","answer":"One sport I've never done but would like to try is rock climbing. I first learned about rock climbing from documentaries and social media platforms showcasing climbers scaling breathtaking rock faces in exotic locations."},{"id":"old-124","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe an advertisement you’ve seen that you didn’t like.","answer":"One advertisement I saw that I didn't like was for a fast-food chain promoting their new burger. I first encountered it while watching TV during primetime. The advertisement featured flashy visuals of the burger, accompanied by upbeat music and exaggerated claims about its taste and quality."},{"id":"old-125","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe a website you often visit.","answer":"One website I frequently visit is Reddit, a social news aggregation and discussion platform. I initially discovered Reddit through a friend who recommended it to me as a great source for diverse content and discussions."},{"id":"old-126","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe a good decision made by someone you know recently.","answer":"A close friend of mine recently made the decision to quit her corporate job and pursue her passion for photography full-time. She had been working in finance for several years but always felt unfulfilled."},{"id":"old-127","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe something/a subject you want to/would like to learn in the future.","answer":"One subject I would like to learn in the future is graphic design. I'm interested in learning how to create visually appealing designs for various purposes, such as advertisements, websites, and branding materials."},{"id":"old-128","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe a daily routine you do.","answer":"One daily routine that I enjoy is practicing mindfulness meditation in the morning. I started following this routine about a year ago after reading about the benefits of mindfulness for mental health and well-being."},{"id":"old-129","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe a time when you heard good news (from someone with a good relationship).","answer":"I vividly remember a sunny afternoon a few months ago when I received a call from my best friend, Sarah. It was around midday, and I was working on some tasks at home. As soon as I heard her voice, I could tell she was brimming with excitement."},{"id":"old-130","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe a time when you missed or were late for an important meeting/event.","answer":"I vividly remember a time when I forgot an important appointment, causing me to be late for a meeting. It happened last year when I was supposed to attend a job interview for a position I was really excited about."},{"id":"old-131","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe a time when you showed something new to others (e.g. family or friends).","answer":"I recall a time when I taught my younger brother how to ride a bicycle. He had been eager to learn for some time, and I decided to take on the task of teaching him."},{"id":"old-132","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe a time when you took a risk.","answer":"One significant risk I took was when I decided to quit my stable job to pursue entrepreneurship. It was about two years ago when I made this decision."},{"id":"old-133","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe an occasion that you needed to wear your best clothes.","answer":"On a particularly special occasion, I recall the time when I was invited to attend a formal wedding ceremony. The grandeur and elegance of the event required me to dress to the nines."},{"id":"old-134","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe a time you got something you wanted.","answer":"A memorable occasion when someone gave me something I really wanted was when my best friend surprised me with a guitar for my birthday. It was a Saturday evening, just before my 25th birthday, and the gift arrived in a beautifully wrapped box."},{"id":"old-135","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe an enjoyable journey by public transport.","answer":"One of the most enjoyable journeys I've ever had was on a train to the charming city of Edinburgh. It was a day trip that I took with my family, and we were all eager to explore the historical city and its unique culture."},{"id":"old-136","set":"2024 Sep–Dec (carried over)","question":"Describe a time you did something that made you feel proud.","answer":"One time that made me feel really proud was when I successfully organized a charity event at my university. This happened during my final year, and I was leading a student group that wanted to raise funds for a local children’s hospital."}];
